WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.034
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:04.637
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At-Home Edition."

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.838
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.107
This is Franny Fallon.
This is Winnie Fallon,

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:11.510
and my wife is
the camera operator today.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.513
Guys, we are --

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.182
April 15th, today is, Wednesday,

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.283
and hopefully you're
doing your part

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.719
and staying at home like we are.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:24.490
If you are going out,
make sure to wear a mask, right?

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.794
And if you -- If you don't
have a mask, you can make one.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.429
There's a lot of things online.
You can learn how to do it.

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:31.765
I saw a cool thing.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.567
Matthew McConaughey
used a bandanna

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.568
and put a coffee filter
in the bandana

00:00:36.568 --> 00:00:39.105
and used that to make
a face mask with rubber bands.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.974
That's pretty cool, right?

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:45.678
We have a big show today.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.413
Pharrell Williams
is on the show,

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.415
very talented Pharrell Williams.
We love him.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:54.653 line:0%
Also, his charity is
World Central Kitchen,

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:56.723 line:0%
wck.org.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:59.425 line:0%
He's doing stuff
with José Andrés.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.427 line:0%
That's a picture
of a dinosaur, right?

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:02.729 line:0%
Or is that a duck?

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.397 line:0%
-Dinosaur.
-Oh, okay.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.766 line:0%
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.269 line:0%
-And then we have
Millie Bobby Brown,

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:14.073 line:0%
who we love,
and her charity is unicef.org.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.542
Speaking of charities,
by the way,

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:17.843
a lot of people
have been stepping up,

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.078
and I think it's a great thing,

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.313
so thank you, everyone,
for donating.

00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:23.282
And my family's donating

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:24.918
to every charity
that we mention on our show,

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.086
but our friends over at T-Mobile

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:28.921
wanted to do something
really cool.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:34.927 line:0%
If you text "THANKS" to 50555,

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.562 line:0%
they're going to --

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:40.366 line:0%
You'll donate $5 to the Boys
and Girls Club of America.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.769 line:0%
Right now, they have a COVID-19
relief fund for front-line --

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:46.439
people working on the front line
for childcare for them,

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.473
'cause they're working
all the time.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.208
-Are you doing this one, Winnie?

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.844
-Yeah, are you?

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:53.513
-No, I'm doing
the princess, though.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:57.149
-And, so, anyways, these people
have to take care of their kids,

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.919
so this will help.
So, if you go to your phone,

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:02.288
I'm using my phone to film,

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:08.494 line:0%
but if you go to your phone
and text "THANKS" to 50555,

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:12.298 line:0%
T-Mobile said they will match
up to $400,000

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.834 line:0%
in the next three days.
That's a lot of money.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.769 line:0%
So that's today,
tomorrow, and Friday,

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.472 line:0%
if you text "THANKS" to 50555

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.375 line:0%
they will automatically
bill you $5.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:27.413
Right?

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:30.616
And there you go.
Did you draw this?

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:33.952
No. Winnie, did you draw this?

00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:36.022
-Yes. So, yeah.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.224
-Who is it?

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.694
-It's two of my classmates.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.295
-I thought it was me and Mommy.

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:45.798
-No.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.100
They're both girls.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.302
They can't be.

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:51.771
-Well, this one's --

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.740
Which -- Who's this one?

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.342
-One that Mommy knows.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.177
-Oh, okay.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.812
I thought it was Daddy
and Mommy, and I thought...

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.281
-Amara.
-...Daddy had, like,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.882
a little cloud over his head
or something.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.017
-Amara.
-Yeah, that's Amara.

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:06.286
-That's Amara.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.387
-Oh, okay, that's Amara.
-That's Audrey.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.123
-Okay, good. It's your friends.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:14.760
Okay. So this is not
me or your mom.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.130
I thought you loved me so much,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.631
I thought maybe you'd draw
a nice picture of me,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.467
but what are you going to do?

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:25.504
Okay, guys.
It is time for monologue.

00:03:25.504 --> 00:03:27.440
Can you guys clap?
You guys like monologue?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.175
-Unh-unh.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:32.978
-Here we go.
-[ Blows raspberry ]

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:34.747
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At-Home Edition."

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.983
Well, guys, today was
supposed to be Tax Day,

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.585
but it was all postponed
until July 15th.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:41.053
The kids are excited

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.655
'cause now we get to leave all
of our Tax Day decorations up

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:46.259
for another three months.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.794
Who wants to light
the W-2 forms?

00:03:48.794 --> 00:03:51.631
I do. I do.
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.535
Tax Day is now
after the 4th of July

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:58.404
which means a lot of Americans
will be able to claim

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:01.741
their fingers and eyebrows
as a total loss.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.109
Some 2020 news --
It was a big day for Joe Biden

00:04:04.109 --> 00:04:06.913
as he picked up an endorsement
from Elizabeth Warren.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:10.016
In the past few days, Biden's
been endorsed by Bernie Sanders,

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.884
President Obama,
and Elizabeth Warren

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.819
while Trump just laughed
and said,

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:17.189
"But look who's got
the MyPillow guy."

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:19.158
I saw that Sony and PlayStation
have started

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.127
the Play at Home initiative

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:24.296
to encourage gamers
to stay indoors.

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.098
Yeah, that's always been
the problem with gamers --

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.468
They spend
too much time outside.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:33.673
I saw the State of New Jersey
is holding a benefit show

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.709
called Jersey for Jersey.
It's the only benefit show

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.911
where the host threatens you
with a baseball bat.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:42.080
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.583
It's the only benefit show
where you send a donation,

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.619
and they say, "Eh."

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.855
-[ Blows raspberry ]

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:52.758
-They say, "Eh, feels light."

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:55.527
The envelope feels light.

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:57.697
I read that a lot of colleges
are starting to think

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:00.400
that classes won't be in person
this fall.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.768
It's awkward when you do your
fraternity initiation over Zoom,

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:05.605
and you have to ask your dad to
smack your butt with a paddle.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:09.074
[ Chuckles ]

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.476
Yeah, that's right,
'cause of the virus,

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.278
kids applying
to college this fall

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:15.481
might not have to submit
S.A.T. scores.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.984
In response, Lori Loughlin
texted Felicity Huffman,

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:21.820
"You've got to be F'ing
kidding me."

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.989
Here's some news
for "Jeopardy!" fans.

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:26.626
I saw that -- Sorry.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:27.993
-Here's some news
for "Jeopardy!" fans.

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:30.462
I saw that Alex Trebek
is releasing a memoir.

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:33.098
Meanwhile, if you like "Wheel of
Fortune," Pat Sajak is releasing

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:35.535
one of those books
that float in the bathtub.

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.770
[ Chuckles ]

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.338
And finally --

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.040
Oh.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.043
Here's the cover
of the "Wheel of Fortune" book.

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:48.947
Finally, I saw that many people
are actually getting dumped

00:05:48.947 --> 00:05:52.751
via Zoom, and it's created
the term "getting Zumped."

00:05:52.751 --> 00:05:55.054
Don't confuse that with a Zump,

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.522
when is when you forget
your camera's on

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.291
when you take your phone
into the bathroom.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.959
That's our monologue, everybody.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.293
Yahoo!

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:02.862
Now we're going to do our thing

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.130
that we've been doing
every Wednesday

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.066
where I look through
the Internet and try to find

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.835
fun things that people are doing
while being quarantined.

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:12.304
It is called,
"What Are You Doing Wednesday."

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:14.673 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:16.041
I just want to show everyone
what you did

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:18.277
to "The Incredibles."

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:21.613
You took all their clothes off.
The naked Incredibles.

00:06:21.613 --> 00:06:23.649
Where's his clothes?

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.155
-[ Giggles ]

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:34.827
[ Giggles ]

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:38.264
-Alright. Take
"The Incredibles." Go play.

00:06:40.365 --> 00:06:43.569
Guys, this is called
"What Are You Doing Wednesday."

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.770
Here's our first one here.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.305
This one's really funny, guys.

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:48.707
This is from
@parmesan-underscore-official.

00:06:48.707 --> 00:06:50.075
They got bored in quarantine,

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:53.178
so she decided to do
the apple fork challenge

00:06:53.178 --> 00:06:55.982
where you throw an apple,
and you catch it on a fork,

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:57.583
and she did it like three times.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.651
Watch.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:05.657 line:0%
-Yes.

00:07:05.657 --> 00:07:08.894 line:0%
Yes.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:11.697 line:0%
Yes!

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.132 line:0%
Yes!

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:14.566
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:15.968
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.370
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.305
-[ Laughs ]
That was really funny, right?

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:21.474
The next one is called
Car Door Ride.

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:24.276
This one is from
@rachel.thomas91.

00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:28.413
She caught her son taking an
unexpected ride in the driveway.

00:07:28.413 --> 00:07:29.815 line:0%
Watch this kid.

00:07:29.815 --> 00:07:32.685 line:0%
[ Wagner's "Ride
of the Valkyries" playing ]

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:38.190 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.225
Watch, he starts flying.

00:07:40.225 --> 00:07:41.960 line:0%
[ Wagner's "Ride
of the Valkyries" playing ]

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.095
He's holding on to the --

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:44.897
The thing picks him up
in the air.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:48.501
[ Laughs ]

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.769
-I like the other one more.

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:52.271
-Yeah.
-Me, too.

00:07:52.271 --> 00:07:53.539
-Well, I thought
that was pretty good.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:57.710
He looked like Jack-Jack.
Now do you like it?

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.378
I thought it was funny.

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:02.448
Our last one here is called
Megaphone Neighbor.

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:08.054
This one is from @gracecuratolo.

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:11.857
Her neighbor gave an impassioned
speech to her block.

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:13.191 line:0%
Take a look at this.

00:08:13.191 --> 00:08:18.364 line:0%
-I just want you to know
that I miss you and I love you!

00:08:18.364 --> 00:08:22.401 line:0%
Can't wait for this [bleep] show
to be over

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:26.772 line:0%
so that I can touch people,
drink with people,

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:30.075 line:0%
and have the best life ever!

00:08:30.075 --> 00:08:33.279 line:0%
-Miss you, too, Tracy!

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:34.647
-Very nice!

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:36.749
Nice use of that megaphone
right there.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.550
Guys, I got my wife's phone,

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.587
so I'm actually going
to do this, text "THANKS"

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:47.126 line:0%
to 50555.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:52.164 line:0%
T-Mobile's helping
with the Girls and Boys Club.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:54.367 line:0%
50555,

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:57.102 line:0%
and all you do
is you text "THANKS."

00:08:57.102 --> 00:08:59.938 line:0%
"To complete your $5 donation
to Boys and Girls Club,

00:08:59.938 --> 00:09:04.109 line:0%
reply with your five-digit
billing ZIP Code."

00:09:04.109 --> 00:09:06.812 line:0%
I lost Franny. Alright.

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:09.482 line:0%
I'm going to say my ZIP Code.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:11.283 line:0%
"Thanks. $5 charged
to phone bill."

00:09:11.283 --> 00:09:13.018 line:0%
Perfect. It works.

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:15.654 line:0%
Guys, we'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:16.689 line:0%
Come on back.

